{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977336-setting-crossover-city","id":977336,"title":"Setting - Crossover City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T13:14:07-07:00","id":977336,"title":"Setting - Crossover City","content":"So, each game-line (other than Beast, maybe) is developed from the perspective that it is the only thing <i>guaranteed</i> to exist in its setting. So, let's make that concept concrete. There are number of parallel Earths, each one almost exactly like the others but for the presence of their specific supernatural group and its related phenomena, and each separate from the others... except, recently, for one city. <hr /><br /> <u><i>A few years ago</i></u>, the Convergence happened, making <i><u>The City</u></i> a meeting point for all manner of mysterious monsters. But strangely, only <i><u>The City</u></i> - the entire rest of the various Earths remain the sole domain of their respective creatures. Only in the <i><u>The City</u></i>, shared across the many realities, can a Vampire run into a Werewolf, or a Mage study a Promethean. Now, each group seeks to carve out their own section of this melting pot, and learn what they can of these strange new beings they've suddenly encountered. <hr /><br /> So, given this justification for why each supernatural splat suddenly find themselves meeting the other with no prior exposure, how does everyone else think things would progress? Any entertaining stories of &quot;First Contact&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>This</u></i> was for text that is deliberately vague and flexible. Fill in as needed/desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:23:40-07:00","id":977339,"title":"","content":"I think Hunters would be interesting in this setting and would, to a degree, have something of an upper hand. They've spent their nights hunting monsters like these. Not the same, but LIKE these. And while the kindred and werewolves and ghosts that they encounter aren't quite the same, they're close enough that they do have techniques for interacting with them. The less antagonistic groups like the Null Mysteriis could likely serve as brokers between organizations, and the more aggressive groups are probably forced to take on different and more politically strategic policies now that they're facing creatures that are more formalized and organized than the stew of bizarre monsters they used to encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:14:13-07:00","id":977387,"title":"","content":"I think to play up the elements at the core of the CoD (localized rather than global conspiracies), I'd segregate The City from the rest of the world. It exists in physical space, but it's not a known quantity. People end up there, but they never seem to leave, and while those in the US and abroad know that The City exists, they never really talk about it except in passing. They mention that the beloved aunt they grew up with lives there now, but they never seem to find the time to visit. It might show up in Forbes lists of the most prominent US cities, but it's never on a listicle for top places to take a vacation. Truck drivers come through, drop off their wares, and go back on their way, their memories of The City fading to a dim reflection miles out.<br /> <br /> A construct fashioned by the God-Machine perhaps? I'm imagining a strange place, the geography of which seems to alter on a whim, even as it holds its integrity from a helicopter view. It's cobbled together from memories of other cities, some strange amalgam of architectural and pop culture flourishes from throughout the ages, but there's a distinct lack of history to the place. From the Spanish mission on the edge of town to the towering Gothic skyscraper flanked by menacing gargoyles to the claustrophobic warrens of Chinatown, few people can rightly say who built them or when. Maybe it's built from remnants of the Classic World of Darkness, an attempt by some inscrutable being to fashion the quintessential &quot;gothic-punk&quot; setting, or maybe it's debris, the last rubble of a dead universe washed ashore in the world that followed.<br /> <br /> There could be connections between the Circle of the Crone and local werewolves, and certainly between research-oriented hunter groups and mages. And I could definitely see the Ordo Dracul wanting to pick apart a promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-27-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:25:34-07:00","id":977397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977336-setting-crossover-city?p=977387#post977387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think to play up the elements at the core of the CoD (localized rather than global conspiracies), I'd segregate The City from the rest of the world. It exists in physical space, but it's not a known quantity. People end up there, but they never seem to leave, and while those in the US and abroad know that The City exists, they never really talk about it except in passing. They mention that the beloved aunt they grew up with lives there now, but they never seem to find the time to visit. It might show up in Forbes lists of the most prominent US cities, but it's never on a listicle for top places to take a vacation. Truck drivers come through, drop off their wares, and go back on their way, their memories of The City fading to a dim reflection miles out.<br /> <br /> A construct fashioned by the God-Machine perhaps? I'm imagining a strange place, the geography of which seems to alter on a whim, even as it holds its integrity from a helicopter view. It's cobbled together from memories of other cities, some strange amalgam of architectural and pop culture flourishes from throughout the age, but there's a distinct lack of history to the place. From the Spanish mission on the edge of town, the towering Gothic skyscraper flanked by menacing gargoyles, and the claustrophobic warrens of Chinatown, few people can rightly say who built them or when.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's already isolated from the rest of the world by nature of nothing from &quot;other&quot; Earths can reach beyond the The City itself. But if you want it completely &quot;extra-territorial&quot;, than can work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:27:59-07:00","id":977399,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Begotten might be both pleased by and useful to this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:30:10-07:00","id":977401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977336-setting-crossover-city?p=977397#post977397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's already isolated from the rest of the world by nature of nothing from &quot;other&quot; Earths can reach beyond the The City itself. But if you want it completely &quot;extra-territorial&quot;, than can work too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thought is that it sits somewhere in the Midwest of each world. No one really talks about it, in much the same way that no one seems to have much to say about, like, Kansas City, but it's there. It shows up on atlases and in census reports, but those who pass through very rarely feel the urge to stay, and almost no one decides to actively journey there without having much active reason to (short of having accrued quite a bit of mystical knowledge to break the veil of disinterest that hangs over the city). Imagine stacking up a whole bunch of identical world maps and then driving a pin through them all, located somewhere in the middle of nowhere. That's The City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}